1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:05,240
Hello, this is BBC Learning English.\h
In today's Phrasal Verbs with Georgie,\h\h

2
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:16,680
we're looking at the phrasal verbs related to\h
'health and fitness'. Are you ready? Let's go!

3
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:20,840
'warm up' means 'doing some light exercise and /or\h\h

4
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:25,360
some stretches to prepare the\h
body for some heavy exercise'.

5
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:29,480
'It's a good idea to warm up\h
before doing an intense workout.'

6
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:34,280
After you’ve 'warmed up', you're ready to\h
'work out', which means 'to train your body\h\h

7
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:39,880
through exercise, often in the gym',\h
but I'm 'working out' in the garden.

8
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:46,040
'I try to work out at least twice a\h
week. It helps to relieve stress.'

9
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:51,720
After 'working out', it's a good idea to\h
'cool down'. This is similar to 'warming up',\h\h

10
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:57,720
but instead of preparing your body for\h
exercise, you're 'recovering from the exercise'.

11
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:59,920
'Don't forget to cool down after doing a workout.'

12
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:06,520
If you 'stick to something', it means 'you\h
continue doing something consistently'. It\h\h

13
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:13,080
comes from the physical sense, so imagine\h
literally sticking to your routine.

14
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:17,120
'I've managed to stick to my running\h
training program for six weeks so far.'

15
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:20,280
If you lose motivation for\h
something and can't 'stick\h\h

16
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:26,760
to' it, you 'give up' - 'you don't\h
continue doing it and accept defeat'.

17
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:32,160
'This exercise routine is too hard. I give up.'

18
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:35,640
Next, we have 'cut down on' and 'cut out'. What's\h\h

19
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:40,120
the difference? If you 'cut down\h
on something', 'you reduce it'.

20
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:46,560
'I've cut down on my caffeine intake, so now I\h
only have three cups of coffee instead of four.'

21
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:51,360
If you 'cut something out'\h
completely, you 'eliminate it'.

22
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:57,720
'I've discovered I'm allergic to nuts, so I\h
have to cut them out of my diet completely.'

23
00:01:57,720 --> 00:02:02,560
Don't 'freak out' and don't 'give up'.\h
Why not try and 'work on' the phrasal\h\h

24
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:12,080
verbs with the free worksheet on\h
our website? See you next time!

